		<description><![CDATA[<p>Madonna could play a key role in an upcoming Frida Kahlo exhibition in Detroit. The Detroit Institute of Arts (DIA) [...]</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonna-could-play-a-key-role-in-an-upcoming-frida-kahlo-exhibition-in-detroit-2015/20140827">Madonna could play a key role in an upcoming Frida Kahlo exhibition in Detroit</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><strong>Madonna could play a key role in an upcoming Frida Kahlo exhibition in Detroit</strong>.</p>
<p>The <strong>Detroit Institute of Arts</strong> (DIA) confirmed in a statement sent to <a href="http://www.mlive.com/entertainment/detroit/index.ssf/2014/08/madonna_detroit_institute_of_a.html" target="_blank">MLive.com</a> that <strong>Madonna</strong> is an avid collector of <strong>Frida Kahlo</strong>, so MLive.com claims that this leads to speculation <strong>Madonna</strong> could be willing to loan part of her <strong>Kahlo</strong> collection to the DIA for an upcoming exhibit called &#8220;Diego Rivera and <strong>Frida Kahlo</strong> in <strong>Detroit</strong>.&#8221; The exhibition will run from March 15 to July 12.</p>
<p>Several attempts by MLive.com to reach <strong>Madonna</strong>&#8216;s publicist Liz Rosenberg were unsuccessful.</p>
<p>Diego Rivera lived with <strong>Frida Kahlo</strong> in <strong>Detroit</strong> in the early 1930s and painted the two iconic Detroit Industry murals that are displayed inside the DIA&#8217;s main entrance. These works of art took most of 1932 and 1933 to create, and they were commissioned Edsel Ford, according to The New Yorker.</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonna-could-play-a-key-role-in-an-upcoming-frida-kahlo-exhibition-in-detroit-2015/20140827">Madonna could play a key role in an upcoming Frida Kahlo exhibition in Detroit</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
