		<description><![CDATA[<p>If you are in Washington DC don&#8217;t forget to visit the exhibition American Cool at the National Portrait Gallery. The [...]</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonna-american-cool-exhibition-washington-dc/20140718">&#8220;Madonna is the epitome of Cool&#8221; &#8211; Don&#8217;t forget to visit the exhibition American Cool</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></description>
				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>If you are in Washington DC don&#8217;t forget to visit the exhibition <strong>American Cool</strong> at the National Portrait Gallery. The exhibit looks back at the stars who have shaped and embodied the concept of cool through 100 photographs of icons including <strong>Madonna</strong>.</p>
<p>The Alt-100 List recognizes those icons over whom we argued the longest and hardest. These public figures point up the richness and depth of American popular culture.</p>
<blockquote class="pixcode  pixcode--testimonial  testimonial testimonial--small-text">
    <div class="testimonial__content">
<p>Material Girl <strong>Madonna</strong> is the epitome of <strong>cool</strong>. One of the most prominent cultural icons for over three decades, the singer has achieved an unprecedented level of power and control for women in the entertainment business. Over 30 years in the music industry, the Queen of Pop has sold more than 300 million records worldwide and is recognized as the best-selling female recording artist of all time by Guinness World Records.</p>
</div>

    
        
            <div class="testimonial__author-name">American Cool</div>
        
        
        
    </blockquote>

<p>“What do we mean when we say somebody is cool in America?” is the question the exhibition elicits.</p>
<p>The photograph of <strong>Madonna</strong> exhibited at <strong>American Cool</strong> is by Kate Simon (1983), see above.</p>
<p>Other singers included on the 100 Coolest American are Prince, Elvis Presley, Jimi Hendrix, Lou Reed, Frank Sinatra, Patti Smith, Bruce Springsteen, James Brown, Kurt Cobain, Bob Dylan, Missy Elliott, Marvin Gaye, Debbie Harry and Neil Young.</p>
<p>The post <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com/madonna-american-cool-exhibition-washington-dc/20140718">&#8220;Madonna is the epitome of Cool&#8221; &#8211; Don&#8217;t forget to visit the exhibition American Cool</a> appeared first on <a rel="nofollow" href="http://drownedmadonna.com">Madonna news new album Rebel Heart</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
